const items0 = [["HG02+03-refix", () => "The table of contents is hiding on the left\n\nSubstack kinda hides the table of contents until you move the mouse toward the left side of the page. On a guide this long, that little hidden menu is your friend.\n\nIntroduction\n\nHello Lovey Bunny!\n\nHave you ever realized that you were born with an incredible brain/mind that has many layers of consciousness: dream, protect, analyze, imitate, love, remember, hide, show, heal, etc, etc?\n\nYet you were taught (or you figured out) that the way to \u2018grow up\u2019 and be an \u2018adult\u2019 is to push through, repress, supress, pretend you\u2019re confident, follow authority, go against authority, etc etc etc, and mind you deeper mind is still running all of the programs it\u2019s running: child mind, guard mind, body mind, intuitive mind, fantasy mind (trying to become guidance mind), etc etc\n\nWhile some of the teachings on hypnosis talk about the \u2018subconscious mind\u2019 like it\u2019s one giant machine you just have to put the right commands into in order to get it to do what you want, for me, the most useful thing to do is talk to the different parts of myself until they can all hear each other.\n\nI teach a self-hypnosis method that allows you to gather all of your attention and have your conscious mind, subconscious mind, body mind, inner child mind, protector part minds, adult mind and Higher Self be able to all hear and talk to each other.\n\n\u201cHow do I do this?\u201d you ask. Just listen. When you warm up to what\u2019s there, protect it, clarify what it is, reality test it, and then act on it, you\u2019ll find that you don\u2019t even need to have a \u2018trance experience\u2019 to demonstrate the results of all parts of your mind talking to each other and trusting each other more.\n\nI like to think of it like a \u2018communion\u2019 between all parts of our mind, where the conscious mind doesn\u2019t have to shout from the roof top and the subconscious mind doesn\u2019t have to manifest symptoms, dreams, cravings, day dreams and weird body signals in order to communicate.\n\nI work with the subconscious as if it were a ecology, and often begin hypnosis working with the Higher Self (universal heart) and only separate into parts when needed. I combine this with inner child reparenting, and also aspects of prompt engineering, as well as helping people to be literate in the domain of what\u2019s hypnotizing them.", "ef7f13929461eba79f607db6e08bd40a958fa963599f08f7e923257f0326908d"], ["HG10-refix", () => "Hypnosis Evidence\n\nIs there REAL (not magical) evidence for Hypnosis? Yes. In 2024 there has been an overview of 49 meta analyses containing a total of 261 distinct primary studies. Evidence was strongest for pain, medical procedures, and work with children and adolescents, but varied with different outcomes and study design quality.\n\nIs there evidence for Self-Hypnosis? Yes. There has been a systematic review of Randomized Controlled Trials of self-hypnosis, finding benefit in studies of pain, child birth, pediatric, stress, anxiety etc. Self-hypnosis seemed more useful when done as a real self-skill several times, not just listening to an audio file.\n\nHere I will be teaching you a real self-skill, so you don\u2019t end up a consumer of more and more elaborate trance recordings.\n\nThe Mayo Clinic warns that using hypnosis to deal with earlier life stressful events may invoke strong emotions and that there are other types of treatments that may be more helpful with historical trauma.\n\nDO use Self Hypnosis to help you: regulate your self, talk to your self, re-parent your self, gain clarity, change habits, make your life safer in the now, integrate emotions, and take action in ordinary life.\n\nDO NOT use Self Hypnosis to help you: force yourself to remember trauma, force yourself to \u201cprove\u201d trauma through memories, suppress medical symptoms, de-stabilize your self, or NOT seek correct treatment.", "bd8e00fc57ebcd9c0f7e182889bd74e960a9cb5b418f0e9c4df04ce6bff99b07"], ["HG11-refix", () => "Forget the left-brain/right-brain cartoon\n\nI use the expression \u2018syncing the hemispheres\u2019 but don\u2019t want to over interpret what is going on neuroscientifcally. A huge study of resting state fmri scans of 1011 people does not support the common pop neuropsych notion that people in general are left or right brained. But there is evidence for lateralisation of some functions or networks.\n\nLet\u2019s elicit a high level of co-operation between the verbal, the analytical, the imaginal, the emotional, the somatic, the intuitive, the relational, the spiritual \u2026 It\u2019s not an electoral process. Nobody needs to win!\n\nThe mind of love and the mind of analysis can BOTH be there - warmth and brightness. The mind of intuition and the mind of rationality can BOTH be there - intuitive signals and testing of those signals without dogma or killing them. The body can have a voice - saying yes or no or not yet. The imagination can have opened up the field and then the adult can choose what to do next in the real world\u2026. It can be peaceful but also precise.\n\nWithout the mind of love the mind of analysis can be sterile. Without the mind of analysis the mind of love can lead to fantasy. Without testing intuitive signals they can become delusions. Without intuitive signals the testing can be dead. So these \u2018modes\u2019 can correct each other.\n\nAnd it\u2019s got to lead somewhere!", "a0fbade1c58c2c07a169a0c4452e7c174b26add36b98947a00fbe42ed951b7bf"], ["HG13-refix", () => "A useful map of the mind\n\nNote: whenever I refer to the \u2018subconscious\u2019 I\u2019m referring to all of the processes under the surface of your conscious awareness: perceptions, emotions, desires, avoidance tendencies, imagery, memories, body signals, habits, intuitions, automatic behaviours and so forth. You can work with all of these together as if it\u2019s all one \u2018mind\u2019, or you can work with it as a set of parts, an \u2018ecology\u2019 if you like. There isn\u2019t a \u2018right\u2019 or \u2018wrong\u2019 way to approach it. They\u2019re all maps. Don\u2019t form a priesthood around either one!\n\nWorking with parts: Precision. Working with Higher Self: Coherence. Doing both: Communion.\n\nIf you need to work with the \u2018whole\u2019, the subconscious as one:\n\na) \u2018Invoke\u2019 the subconscious in some way. Something simple like \u2018Hello, wise subconscious\u2026\u2019 or whatever works for you.\n\nIf you need to work with the \u2018ecology\u2019 in the subconscious (child parts, protectors, \u2018critic\u2019, fantasy making parts, body memories, social part, spiritual part (God/source/best benefit of all beings part) \u2018wiser\u2019 part etc etc then:\n\na) It\u2019s usually a good idea to start with unity. So \u2018invoke\u2019 your Higher Self: Hello my Higher Self/universal heart-mind/wise subconscious\u2026\n\nb) Move into differentiation. \u201cWhich part is afraid? Which part wants to protect you? Which part wants to avoid it? Which part knows what to do? Which part is too young for this?\u201d Etc.\n\nc) Move back into unity again. \u201cAnd all of these parts are part of the one life, and as the adult in charge of this life you can lead with love, knowing that all of these parts are part of your life\u2026\u201d Etc.\n\nSometimes start with the whole\n\nSometimes, it\u2019s better to start with the whole.\n\nSome people make themselves too fragmented by starting to work with parts. \u2018Here\u2019s a part! Here\u2019s another one! I\u2019ll get twelve of them in a room and give them all an office to hang around in!\u2019 So it\u2019s better to start from the Sacred.\n\nStart like this: \u2018I\u2019m approaching this from the universal heart. I\u2019m approaching this from my Higher Self. I\u2019m approaching this from the part of me that knows it belongs to life, not any wound, or role, or family, or group, or identity, or ideology, or story. So can you please tell me what\u2019s going to be true and kind and timely and stabilising and useful here?\u2019 Etc.\n\nIt can be that you can\u2019t even access your Higher Self, or the universal heart, or whatever works for you. (Btw, if it doesn\u2019t work for you don\u2019t use it! It\u2019s no good adopting somebody else\u2019s map.) In that case, start by just witnessing whatever is coming up. Notice the room, your body, the fact that you\u2019re in a younger state etc.\n\nOnce you have the ability to notice, and to differentiate, you don\u2019t need to keep rehearsing it. Just work on whatever it is you need to work on (often warming up and protecting yourself and knowing what to do etc). So even though it can be useful to talk about your Higher Self, it doesn\u2019t mean you already have all the good inner parenting functions etc that you need. You usually need to work on developing them.\n\nDifferentiate only as you need to. \u201cIs this my inner child? Or is this a protector? Is this my body? Is this fear? Is this intuition? Is this my social part? Is this divine guidance, or is this my interpretation of divine guidance?\u201d\n\nAlways start from the heart, differentiate when you need to, then come back to the heart again.", "f82b236267c00c0df345362fe27e8747244a71ed93a979136dcde2f09468aa6f"], ["HG14-refix", () => "The inner child, the guards, and the three inner adults\n\nYour inner child won\u2019t trust you right away. It\u2019s not going to be enough for you to meditate, say three nice sentences to the inner child and expect to have its trust. What\u2019s going to help your inner child to trust you is you, the person you are right now, becoming reliable.\n\nHere I\u2019m going to talk about what you need to develop in yourself in order to be able to reparent your inner child. I\u2019m going to talk about it in terms of three aspects: your Nurturer, your Protector and your Leader/Guru, but I don\u2019t mean them as if there were really three people in you. It\u2019s you that needs to develop these qualities.\n\nAlso, your inner child\u2019s worth is not dependent on these qualities\u2026 It has its own worth, and its own qualities, like playing, being tender, not taking life too seriously, being creative and wondering at the world. Those belong in your relationship with it too, not just the wounds.\n\nWhen the adult role is not available yet\n\nThe problem is, that some people do not have access to their adult functions at will. Instead, they may go blank, access an inherited inner critic, or feel like a child part who may be playing at being an adult. Telling them to just access their adult is like telling them to just be able to fly.\n\nFor that starting point, I use a provisional bridge I developed and call borrowed adulthood. Please note, it puts together familiar practices (witnessing, modeling, supported action, and handing over responsibility bit by bit), and I\u2019m not claiming that the entirety of the steps has been validated as one treatment.\n\n- Access a witnessing position, if necessary: notice what\u2019s there without demanding warmth, wisdom or certainty. If you already know how to distinguish your internal positions, skip to the next step and access the adult position you need.\n\n- Borrow an adult function. You may \u201cborrow\u201d this from a safe adult in your life, a mentor, an older sibling, a future version of yourself, a spiritual figure, a value, or even a written plan. Borrow only what you need right now \u2013 warmth, a boundary or direction.\n\n- Put on the adult hat as an apprentice. Now, in this position, figure out what you would want to say or do \u2013 and then do at least a part of that.\n\n- Return the adult hat, noticing what you borrowed and what you were able to do on your own (even if it\u2019s only 5%).\n\nThis is a borrowed figure, so you\u2019re still making the choice. The longer version of this exercise can be found in my Inner Child Self-Love Reparenting Guide .\n\nYou don\u2019t have to have trustworthy people in your history. Use someone you remember when that helps, or just imagine a good adult whose intention is to take good care of you. See if you can imagine what they would say/do in your situation, with your history, limitations, options, etc. If you can\u2019t imagine good, start with the least cruel response you can believe. Once you\u2019ve found something good, try it, don\u2019t keep doing the exercise.\n\nIt can be helpful to use borrowing when you\u2019re in the adult position and not knowing what a decent adult would do, especially when the child doesn\u2019t trust you and every response you can think of is retaliating, defending your goodness, collapsing or leaving. How would a decent adult hear that distrust? Borrow that one response. You may still feel young when you do it, it\u2019s okay, feeling like an adult can come after you act like one.\n\nLet the child speak without handing over the steering wheel\n\nIt\u2019s possible to let the \u2018younger\u2019 parts of you express themselves without surrendering your adult judgement to them, and without literally reverting to a younger age. Instead, the aim is to access the positive aspects of \u2018younger\u2019 feeling states, such as a sense of wonder or playfulness, more direct sensory experiences, vulnerability, need, and a desire to let someone else make decisions for you.\n\n\"It is okay for a younger part of me to talk. But I understand that the adult in me is always going to be here, listening, evaluating, protecting me and stopping me if needed. I am not going to replace my adult judgement with any child state, guide, recording or person.\"\n\nThis way you get the benefits of being young; curiosity, spontaneity, play, sensation, the ability to state your needs, to feel easily etc without any of the negatives of being a child, like obeying, being helpless, being scolded, the lack of good judgement etc.\n\nLove doesn\u2019t have to wait for trust\n\nEven if your inner child does not believe that you love him or her, you can still love him or her.\n\nYou can say, out loud or in your head, \u201cOkay. I believe that you don\u2019t believe me, but I still love you. You don\u2019t have to love me back. Please tell me what is not okay with you.\u201d\n\nRespond to complaints, which are likely to include something true. Showing that you love him or her can include some or all of the following: listening to him or her when he or she is angry without hitting back, owning up to what was not okay, working on being less likely to turn on him or her, and other ways of making it up to him or her. Other ways of showing that you love him or her include taking care of him or her by buying and cooking food, setting limits, taking him or her to doctor\u2019s appointments, and doing what you say you will do. Just not hitting back is not enough; you also need to love your inner child.\n\nBe aware of what you are teaching your other positions. You might be teaching your inner child that you are going to love him or her no matter what, but you might also be teaching him or her that he or she is responsible for believing your love, and that if he or she does not, it is his or her fault. The position that is making the vow to love the inner child no matter what, and the position that is blaming the inner child for not taking in the love, might be separate positions, or they might be one position, or you might be blending them. It might not be based on chronological age.\n\nWhen you're placing your younger self on trial, how valuable is it for you to consider how valuable it might have been for your younger self at the time to be doing what they did, given what they knew at the time? How valuable is it for you to consider how valuable it might have been for them to think what they thought, given what they thought at the time? How valuable is it for you to consider what options were available to them at the time, and how tolerable they were? How valuable is it for you to consider the consequences of their actions at the time? How valuable is it for you to consider that whilst their actions might have caused harm to you and others, punishing yourself now will not give them the capacity they needed at the time, and that it is more useful to work on what you can do now to deal with the harm that was caused?\n\nWORKING WITH YOUR INNER CHILD:\n\nThe two-hand practice\n\nThere is a simple and easy body technique to connect with your inner child. Just place one hand in the center of your chest which is physically connecting you to your love and then place your other hand just below that which is your solar plexis and where your child can be.\n\nBegin to send love from your heart down to your child and just notice what comes up for you. It doesn't matter if something comes up or not. If you feel resistance, just meet it with love. If you feel or see something, just meet that with love as well. This is a conversation with your child from your heart.\n\nRemember, Love is on top, your child is on the bottom and you are there with them.\n\nThe Nurturer\n\nTHE NURTURER: As a Nurturer one of the most important things that you can do is to enjoy your inner child, to sit back and not feel like you have to move their feelings and to say to them that you are really glad that they are here in this moment. Children need to be enjoyed.\n\nIt\u2019s okay that you\u2019re feeling the way you are feeling.\n\nI want you to know I\u2019m here for you.\n\nYou don\u2019t need to do anything right now.\n\nIt\u2019s okay that you\u2019re not too much. It\u2019s okay to be small. You can be small here.\n\nIt\u2019s okay to be angry. You can be angry here.\n\nIt\u2019s okay to be sad. You can be sad here.\n\nThe Protector\n\nI\u2019m going to be here for you.\n\nThe Protector:\n\nWork with your Protector to set boundaries together. They might be small, like \u201cI\u2019m going to leave this conversation because it\u2019s not safe,\u201d or \u201cI\u2019m going to stop texting someone who destabilizes me.\u201d They might be self-care related, like \u201cI\u2019m going to eat\u201d or \u201cI\u2019m going to get sleep.\u201d They might be trust-related, like \u201cI\u2019m going to keep this promise to myself\u201d or \u201cI\u2019m not going to leave you alone to deal with these adult things.\u201d\n\nA lot of inner child work fails because we do all the fluffy stuff, but then we go text the person who destabilizes us or don\u2019t eat or don\u2019t do whatever thing we were meant to be doing. Trust comes from being able to handle adult things.\n\nIf you can\u2019t bring up the warmth stuff yet, that\u2019s okay, you can always do something to be protective of your inner child. Make sure they\u2019re small enough that you can do them. If you can\u2019t, figure out what\u2019s getting in the way of doing them. Are you scared? Tired? Don\u2019t know how? Is there a practical obstacle in your way? Did you set yourself up to do it successfully? Be careful not to define doing the thing successfully as \u201cfeeling good about it\u201d or \u201cbeing able to check it off a list.\u201d\n\nThe Leader, Guide, or Guru\n\nThe Leader/Guide/Guru:\n\nYou can also work with your Leader. Call them whatever you want, Guide, Guru, Wise One, Sage, Inner Teacher, Director, Higher Adult, whatever.\n\nAsk them for help with directing your life. Be careful not to ask for the kind of \u201ctough it out, you don\u2019t have needs, you just need discipline!\u201d kind of direction, though. Ask them for help in directing you to do adult things in a way that takes your needs into account: asking for the help you need, expressing your preferences, letting someone see you in an imperfect way, finding ways to get your need for closeness met without punishing someone for their need for space, etc. etc.\n\nAffirmations might be helpful here, too: \u201cWe\u2019re not just here to feel good. We\u2019re here to become whole. We\u2019re here to be part of life. We\u2019re here to serve truth/beauty/love/God/source/nature/the universe/dharma/the Tao/the benefit of all beings,\u201d etc. etc.\n\nStart with whatever adult function you can connect to. Even if you start with protection and can\u2019t do the warmth stuff yet, make sure the direction you\u2019re being led in is appropriate for your inner child\u2019s growth (i.e. not depriving them of things they need, like play or support, etc.)\n\nWorking with protectors\n\nWorking with protectors:\n\nFeel free to use parts language here, too, if it\u2019s helpful. Often, we see a sensation or a distraction or an objection as something that needs to be explored, when in fact it might just be hunger, or reasonable skepticism about something, or a sentence that doesn\u2019t fit. It\u2019s good to notice it, though, and then to see what might be going on.\n\nMost people assume when approaching their inner child that the first thing they\u2019ll encounter is\u2026their inner child.\n\nBut more often than not, what you actually experience is numbness, cynicism, anger, hunger, the sudden urge to check your phone, a sexual urge, mental planning, sleepiness, dissociation, or the simple thought that \u201cthis is stupid\u201d. I wouldn\u2019t call those failures. They\u2019re often the protector, the guard at the door, showing up in its usual charming way.\n\nOne important voice to become aware of when approaching your inner child is your inherited parent. This is the voice of your parent(s) that you internalized as a child, based on how they treated you. This is not the same as your inner adult (Nurturer, Protector, Leader/Guru) that you will eventually build up. Often this inherited parent acts as a critic or warden, telling your inner child not to cry, not to be \u201cneedy\u201d, not to embarrass them, not to be too independent, etc. So when you begin talking to your child in a new, loving way, this voice may jump in to say that what you\u2019re doing is \u201cfake\u201d.\n\n(\u201cI notice you and what you are trying to do. I want to know more. Could I ask you what you are afraid would happen if you stopped protecting me by\u2026..?)\n\nIf necessary take time and listen. (Perhaps they are afraid that you will lie to yourself again or pretend again or that it will be too painful or you will get spiritual bypass again or you will forgive someone who shouldn\u2019t be forgiven yet or you will see what you want to see or that you will leave them hanging after the session or\u2026..)\n\n(Now talk to the protector. Tell them that it makes sense that they want to protect you and that they don\u2019t have to stop protecting you, but that you want to know what could make them trust you 1% more that you can do that.)\n\nMost of the time the protector wants you to do certain things, set boundaries, do whatever you are supposed to do, eat, not text someone, keep a promise, go to sleep, talk to the therapist, admit that you owe someone money, write something down, etc.\n\nProtection that knows when to stop scanning\n\nDo you want to \u201cembody\u201d your Protector? Then you could practice this:\n\n1. orient self (look around, feel the support around you, etc.)\n\n2. assess the situation (know what you know, what you don\u2019t know and check out what you need to)\n\n3. differentiate between actual/real danger, unknown, past or imagined dangers\n\n4. set boundaries (start with one and make it relative to the danger; move, stop, delay, ask, leave, get support, etc.)\n\n5. verify if it is safe enough\n\n6. stand down and rest\n\nThis seems to me like a \u201cmature\u201d Protector. One that is not afraid to say that he doesn\u2019t know, or one that can ask another human being, or one that can delay interpreting a situation or one that can use a no-trance method. I want to be able to \u201cdo\u201d this too. I am learning to \u201cdo\u201d discernment when I need to and stop scanning the room when it isn\u2019t needed anymore.\n\nInner child reparenting\n\nI see a lot of connection between reparenting therapy and self hypnosis. They fit well together. When you go into hypnosis the child might come to you. If you want, you can see that child in any form you want. It can be an image, a posture, a voice, a memory, an emotion, etc. It can be any age you want it to be. It can be any vulnerable part of you. It doesn\u2019t even have to be a \u201cchild\u201d, if there is no child there, just work with a protector or whatever you find.\n\nDon\u2019t rush the repair\n\nJust be with the child.\n\nIf you can, tell the child that you are there for them and that they don\u2019t have to explain themselves, or be \u201chealed\u201d or impress you. Just tell you what they need to not be alone anymore.\n\nIt can be anything. What does the child need? warmth, to play, to be protected, to mourn, to be angry, food, rest, boundaries, better relationships, to stop fantasizing, to stop working their butt off, that you keep a promise to them for one day, etc. etc.\n\nDon't rush it.\n\nFind a younger you/protector/feeling/signal that comes up in your body, and\n\nA. Prepare yourself to tend to them (get yourself into a place where you can spend time with them, have privacy, feel you can access support if you need it, and be as adult as you can be).\n\nB. Look at what's there before judging or deciding what it is.\n\nC. Ask them what you can do or if you can move closer to them. If you feel like you already know what they need, tell them that you're going to get them what they need- warmth, space, verbal reassurance, silence, distance, whatever.\n\nD. Give them what you can- don't feel like you have to fix it all.\n\nE. Give yourself some time to let what you did sink in- it may take some time, it may take you to go to sleep, etc.\n\nF. Reconnect with them- don't expect them to merge, go away, forgive you, become happy, etc. Just reconnect with them if they're willing.\n\nG. Rest, and reconnect with them later to see what was helpful.\n\nRemember the goal isn't to make yourself good as new but to make yourself good as you- more supported and connected to yourself. Feel free to modify this as needed, and if you don't like the idea of part work you can substitute whatever part you're working with for a signal or a feeling, or an imaginary younger you that you feel embodies the issue you're having.\n\nPlay and rest still need an adult present\n\nWhen you're reparenting, it's okay to play with things that interest your younger states. Whether that means touching things of different textures, drawing, exercising, roleplaying with a plushie in a different voice, etc. As long as you're reality testing is good and you remember that you aren't a child or pet or doll or whatever and that nobody owns you, it's okay to work on getting your play ability back.\n\nWhen you're resting, you don't have to be helpless. It's okay to cut down the amount of decisions you make for a set period of time, put things you haven't finished on a list where you can see it, and let the adult part of you watch over you.\n\nNon-dominant hand dialogue\n\nIf talking out loud or visualizing conversations feels fake, try writing it out. Tell your child/ protector part to write with your nondominant hand, and talk to them with your dominant. It might be a little hard to write with your nondominant hand but you can kind of do it. So for example, they might say \"I don't trust you\" with your nondominant hand, and you can say with your dominant hand \"I know you don't trust me right now but I love you and I want to know how I've fucked up. I don't expect you to trust me but I want to hear you out and give you a promise I can keep today\" and they can say \"what promise?\" and you can say \"I'm going to make sure I eat today/ clear off my desk/ not text so-and-so\"", "59b333ac3b4252afed0545daa878b4cf6864f0ee0ff65d730bcc5a908997932a"], ["HG15-refix", () => "When \u201cyour voice\u201d is everybody else\u2019s voice\n\nIt can be difficult to connect with your inner child if your inner child didn\u2019t have the opportunity to develop. This happens often when you grow up in a situation where you don\u2019t have a private self, for example when your family, religion, or community \u2018takes over\u2019 very early in your life. Or you are pushed to achieve very early in life. The result is that you don\u2019t know what you feel, what you want, what you believe, what you like and dislike until you have heard someone else\u2019s opinion about it. If you are in that situation, it can be difficult to follow the advice to \u2018love yourself\u2019. You don\u2019t even know who \u2018yourself\u2019 is! So you need to do reparenting and finding yourself in parallel. For others, it is very easy to work with the inner child, they can feel it easily.\n\nYou are in this camp if:\n\nYou don\u2019t know what you want, until you have heard what someone else wants.\n\nYour opinion is very different when you are with different people\n\nYou agree with people at the moment but when you are by yourself you realize that you don\u2019t agree with them\n\nYou take responsibility for the emotions of others, at the expense of yourself\n\nWhen you try to love yourself, it feels more like a show\n\nWhen you try to find out how your inner child feels, you feel that you are guessing instead of feeling\n\nYou can rebel, but you can\u2019t choose\n\nThis happens because when you were a child, you didn\u2019t have the opportunity to explore what you like, what you want to try out and who you are. This is not a criticism of your brain but a practical way to look at it.\n\nSometimes you need to distance yourself for a certain time from the people or group that you normally get your answers from. But not for too long, as then you defeat the purpose of this exercise! You need to differentiate yourself a bit from your social environment.\n\nWhat is the difference between a human doer and a human being? If you don\u2019t feel good enough as a human being, you will try to become good enough as a human doer by for example being beautiful, doing something well, being smart, having a certain status, being spiritual, etc. In these areas, you made a bargain with yourself that as long as you are good in these areas, you will be good enough.\n\nSo in order to find yourself, you can ask yourself:\n\nWhat do I like when nobody is looking?\n\nWhat do I believe when I don\u2019t check with other people?\n\nWhat do I want that is neither in rebellion nor in compliance with others?\n\nWhere am I buying my sense of belonging at the expense of betraying myself?\n\nIn what arena am I trying to buy my sense of belonging?\n\nWhat can I try on that I don\u2019t need to be good at?\n\nWith whom can I be myself?\n\nWhat do I feel in my body and what do I make out of it?\n\nGive your inner child the opportunity to do something that has no value on its own and that it doesn\u2019t need to be good at for its resume. For example painting, dancing, gardening, learning a language, playing a sport, doing volunteer work, playing a musical instrument, etc. Because often your inner parent tells your inner child that it is supposed to be good at something as soon as it starts doing it. And that\u2019s not good because your inner child will get humiliated that it isn\u2019t good at it. So try things out long enough until the humiliation is gone.\n\nWhen you are a child, you will feel that you need to belong to a family in order to survive. That is why many people do things for their family, their religion, their romantic partner, their political tribe, their spiritual group, their institution or their online community that they otherwise wouldn\u2019t do! Part of adulting is finding out where you sell yourself in order to belong, and then making the conscious choice where you want to belong. Because a large part of your subconscious mind, is made out of other people. This is why you are reading a self hypnosis guide!\n\nWhere am I betraying myself in order to belong?\n\nWhat does it feel like to belong without betraying myself?\n\nWhere do I think I am following my own guidance, but I am in fact following my belonging program?\n\nWhere do I think I am doing things out of love, but I am actually doing it out of fear of not belonging?\n\nWhere do I think I am listening to my conscience, but I am actually listening to my conditioning?\n\nWhere do I think I am doing something out of devotion, but I am actually doing it out of compliance?\n\nWhere do I think I am rebelling, but I am actually free?\n\nAnd then look what your body tells you. It is not always correct, but it is a good place to start.", "3ef779ed5ce66846a7e7047095194923190d5471a44381998825785fd7143080"], ["HG18-refix", () => "Come all the way back\n\nMake sure that you come out of the session in reverse to how you got in. If you floated up, float back down the same way and come back down to your chosen weight. If you shrank yourself, make sure that you come back to your normal size. If you went inside to a younger you or parts of you make sure that you know that you are whole now, in your body and with your adult judgement. If you traveled somewhere, come back the same way. Only bring back what you need to bring back.\n\nYou may want to say something like, \"I am only bringing back what I need to bring back at this time. Anything that is not needed by me at this time I will store away safely until such time as I need it. I am coming back now to this place, to my body and to normal day to day living, to doing one honest action at a time. Any instructions that I gave myself to go deeper or to remain in session are now over. (Unless you are giving yourself instructions to implement in ordinary life or to cue practice at a future time, and those instructions should not take you out of ordinary life.) I am me now, in my body, with my adult judgement.\"\n\nThen you might want to count yourself out. \"1 I am coming back now into my body, to my chosen weight. 2 I am coming back to my normal breathing pattern. 3 I am hearing the sounds around me now, I am in (where ever you are). 4 I am moving my fingers and my toes, my shoulders and my eyes. 5 I am opening my eyes now, feeling normal and present. My session is over.\"\n\nWhen you come out make sure that you come all the way out. State to yourself what day it is or what date it is. Look to your left and to your right. Look at something close and something far away. Move about a little bit before you stand up, and only stand up when you feel that you can do so. Make sure that you are alert and oriented. Just because you counted, doesn't mean that you are all the way out. Take note of what you need to do as a result of the session, if anything, and then go about doing something normal.\n\nIn the event that a recording that you are listening to stops, you can say to yourself that the recording has stopped and the session is over and use the above mentioned method to bring yourself out of the session. Open your eyes, state to yourself where you are and what day it is, push down with your feet or your hands, move about, look around and then use the above mentioned 5 step method to bring yourself out. Don't sit there waiting for the recording to \"let you out\" it isn't going to.\n\nNOTE: If you are using a recording to take you to sleep, it is all right to allow the recording to put you to sleep or to allow you to remain in a quiet place. But if it is a recording to be used while awake, it should not put you in a role, it should not take away your judgement, it should not inhibit your movement capabilities, it should not leave you blank, it should not leave you with an undefined reset word and it should not allow you to remain in an altered state for as long as you wish.", "32c382ff3280a2f503683cf2570290d5bcf44ae1db3debbec4a4aa4821b078c8"], ["HG19-refix", () => "The actual inner meeting\n\nNote: If you have a tendency to day dream, dissociate or fall asleep, it is better to do this exercise sitting up until you are ready to try this lying down, either to go to sleep, get a very deep rest or incubate dreams. If you are sitting, keep your spine straight but not rigid like a soldier. Relax your jaw and stay somewhat connected to the room you are in.\n\n\u201cUnless I\u2019m going to sleep or want deep rest, I am not leaving life; I am listening more deeply to life.\n\nI invoke my Higher Self, universal heart-mind, wise subconscious mind, intelligence in my body, inner child(ren), inner adult(s), protector(s) and all that is of truth and love to help me know what I need to know in a form and at a level that will be useful, kind, stabilizing and real for me.\u201d\n\nAsk your conscious mind to listen.\n\nThis does not mean you have to stop thinking to listen. Just notice your thoughts, body sensations, pictures, doubts, emotions, etc. Don\u2019t fight what comes up, but don\u2019t go with it either. Just notice what stands out on its own as you hold the idea of what you are doing in the back of your mind.\n\nInternally say, \u201cTell me what I need to know or ask me what you need to know and I\u2019ll sit in silence for 5 minutes and listen.\u201d\n\nYou may hear a phrase, feel a body sensation, notice a memory, see a color, be contacted by a child or protector, feel pain, warmth, complete silence, know that you need to do something, be grateful for something, feel you need to stop the listening or any number of things.\n\nListen to everything and believe nothing.", "b0c1713226590c9f8559fb6374ca35c9e8a3a33a427b0badbca39250a8e7fbe9"], ["HG20-refix", () => "Let the next response guide you\n\nOnce you've read the induction and done the inner meeting, this will make more sense. Read through these, and then try doing it without looking at the screen.\n\nRespond to each thing that comes up with an accurate notice and a small reasonable invitation (or act or taking more time etc). The 'thing' might be a sensation, image, gesture, feeling, words, or anything. The notice and invitation don't need to take all those forms, just notice and invite what happens.\n\nFinding your own words\n\nAn example notice might be, \"I notice my chest tightening when I imagine asking for help\". Don't add interpretation like \"this must be the abandoned child part of me, or a protective mechanism\" - just notice what you notice. An example invitation might be, \"And as I notice that, I can take some time to decide whether that's accurate or not, and notice if I want to say anything, or change it, or just stay like that\".\n\nThen just listen. You don't need fancy language - often it will be better to just ask what happens next, or whatever. If you notice a feeling developing, it might be best not to say anything while it's developing (if you can help it) but somedays you need to talk to understand, so just do that.\n\nYou can be pretty straightforward when you say you're not going to do something that isn't helping - \"That's not helping, I'm not going to do that anymore.\" can be a perfectly valid thing to say to yourself, and help you focus. It's ok to just be with an unpleasant feeling, you don't have to wait till it's a nice one before you know you're ok. As long as you're ok, and willing to change if you want to, and happy to carry on, a sad feeling or tension or whatever doesn't mean it's not ok.\n\nIt's worth trying to separate the notice, the meaning, and your thoughts on the meaning, but in practice it will often be pretty fuzzy. When you can, it can be helpful to separate it out like that though - \"I noticed... this seemed to mean... here's why that might be true / false\" or something like that.\n\nIs this a notice or meaning? \"My stomach went tight\" is a notice, \"He's a complete bastard\" is a meaning, even if you didn't think it in words. You can then go on to find out what he did, notice what it was that gave you the idea, and consider if there might be other explanations. It's also ok to use phrases that you didn't think in your head - if something comes up that you're analysing, it's still good to analyse, even if it's not in your head already. Nonverbal thoughts and early thoughts aren't necessarily any better or worse than other thoughts. Feelings are good to pay attention to, but it's still good to consider what they mean.\n\nLet the response change the invitation\n\nIf you notice something like your shoulders tightening in response to an invitation, that's different from saying \"that's not quite right\". The first one doesn't tell you why - it's worth considering whether it fits, but if you get a clear 'no' then you don't need any more reason to change what you're doing. If something doesn't fit, change it - don't keep trying the same thing.\n\n\"I notice the tightness, and I can just leave it like that. I wonder if that fits, or if I'd rather do something different?\"\n\nSometimes it just isn't right - sometimes it's something you hadn't thought of. Neither is a protector, and just being silent doesn't mean there's a process.\n\nLook at the situation too\n\nIf there is another person involved in the situation, it may be a good idea to look at what they are doing as well. Are they able to communicate in a mature fashion? Try and be specific in your description, and be willing to alter it if you find out that it was incorrect. Just because someone is disagreeing with you or trying to set boundaries around you does not mean they are in their emotionally immature parts. You don\u2019t need to subject yourself to something that may be dangerous to determine if this is the case.\n\nOn the other hand, you may find that you have acted inappropriately and you feel guilty. Having feelings of guilt does not mean that you have done something wrong or that you have been manipulated. Have you done something that was wrong or that caused harm? If so, what can you do to fix it? On the other hand, did you give in to someone else just to keep them from being disappointed in you? What do you want to do or achieve the next time you interact with this person? Do you need them to understand what you are feeling/thinking? Do you just need to communicate information to them? Do you need to set boundaries with them? Do you need to end the interaction prematurely?\n\nChange the amount of contact\n\nWhen you start to contact it, if it feels too much, immediately start to widen your awareness to something else in the room, in your body, etc. Keep moving back and forth between the difficult thing and the easier thing. This is called pendulation and titration. Do as much or as little as you feel you can. You set the pace, you don\u2019t have to do a certain number.\n\nOk, I think that is enough for now.\n\nFeel free to go back and explore more if you wish to do so. If, at any point, you start to lose contact with the here and now, feel that things are becoming more and more unreal, or you feel that you are not able to switch to something else or stop, stop trying to explore inside of yourself and just do the entire \u201ccoming back\u201d part. If you have trouble orienting yourself and it lasts for a prolonged period of time, please get some human help rather than trying a stronger \u201cinduction\u201d back to the here and now.\n\nIf you feel an urge to move, turn, reach, push, or change your body\u2019s position, feel free to either actually do something that will not cause your body pain or discomfort, or just imagine doing what you feel you need to do, and see what happens next. You do not need to \u201cact out\u201d the urge, feel that you need to move, shake, release, etc. If you do move and you feel that you are causing yourself pain or other symptoms that you are concerned about, stop moving.\n\nOffer the care that is actually wanted\n\nIf any \u201cyounger\u201d parts come up, offer them the opportunity to spend time with you. You don\u2019t have to consider them literally \u201cyounger\u201d, nor do you have to ask them why they are there or what happened to them. If you can identify any \u201cprotector\u201d parts, talk to them and find out what they are concerned about. All of them are welcome to the \u201cmeeting\u201d. You don\u2019t have to get rid of any of them.\n\nIf you feel that it would be useful to bring in a \u201cnurturer\u201d, \u201cprotector\u201d, \u201cleader\u201d, etc to help you either change the \u201ctone\u201d of the interaction, set boundaries, or help you figure out how to live your life in a better fashion, feel free to do so. You don\u2019t have to talk to them, just use them to get whatever function you need that you aren\u2019t able to do on your own. You only need to use the \u201cWitness\u201d if you need help getting started with a step. If you are already able to do a certain step, you don\u2019t have to do it again.\n\nTry some different ideas as to what might be helpful for this \u2018inner part\u2019 to feel better (being welcomed by you, visualising someone else, giving them the sort of words they would like to hear, you placing yourself in a different body position, you moving further away etc). Only try one idea at a time to see if it works. Just because an idea \u2018should\u2019 be a resource, that doesn\u2019t mean that it will be.\n\nIt is possible that when you try and give the part what it wants, you might feel very upset. It may be that it never got what it needed at the time and now that you are giving it what it wants, it is processing the upset of not getting what it wanted before. If this happens, allow yourself to respond for as long as you want to do so, and for as long as you can \u2018stay there\u2019 (ie remain in the process). If you feel that the voice, distance, touch, image etc is too much, then change it to something that is less. Don\u2019t think that you can\u2019t \u2018take\u2019 the love.\n\nAllow yourself to see where the metaphor takes you. Ask questions like \u2018if the problem had an image or story, what would it be?\u2019 or \u2018what would need to happen to make things right?\u2019 If it feels like you need to \u2018do something\u2019 to give yourself the resource that you feel you need (or to put a boundary in place, or to move away or to take some other action) then try \u2018doing that\u2019 for as far as it takes to be of use to you. Remember that whatever you find out, is likely to be metaphorical. It may be a good hypothesis for what you need to do but it is not a proven fact.\n\nAlternatively, you may want to use the session to develop a capacity that you want to develop (ie love, play, courage, curiosity etc). You can also use it to rehearse something that you have decided to do.\n\nFinish without forcing a revelation\n\nEnding the session . Don\u2019t feel that you have to end the session with a \u2018great revelation\u2019! When you have done as much as you want to do, it is a good idea to find out if there is anything that you need to do to make sure that you can leave things where they are for the time being. This might include thanking parts for their help, or making sure that you do something \u2018in real life\u2019 (eat a good meal, put a boundary in place, get some rest, repair a relationship, keep a promise etc) or it may be that there is nothing to do!\n\nNote : throughout the exercise, allow your \u2018analytical\u2019 part to make comments and/or tell you that it doesn\u2019t like what you are doing and/or tell you to stop doing the exercise. Just tell it that you will check things out when you come back and make any commitments etc when you are back. Remember that the images that you see are unlikely to be actual memories of things that happened and just because you see an image, or feel a body release, that doesn\u2019t mean that you are right about what is going on!\n\nWhen you have finished, even if you stopped part way through, use the \u2018 Come all the way back \u2018 procedure to bring yourself back. When you are back, it is a good idea to write a few lines in a notebook about what you have done. Just jot down the essentials (what was there before you started, what you have done to change things, what you are unsure about, any phrases that were said, any body signals, any information that the \u2018inner child\u2019 said that it needed, anything that a \u2018protector\u2019 wanted you to know, any boundaries that you put in place, any \u2018repairs\u2019 that you did, anything that you learnt about what it is a mistake to try and force etc). You don\u2019t need to write down the whole cast of characters, just what you actually", "434932a959142fb113036d254379d541c346d8682a2fa60c011aaf09da3ed698"], ["HG21-refix", () => "The 15-minute daily practice\n\nNotice there is no need to learn a second script! The process is the same. You are simply practicing for fifteen minutes or so. That is long enough to induce yourself (it only takes a few minutes), practice for a short time (five minutes is plenty to see what happens when you simply sit in silence, listening, and you can interrupt yourself at any time to change direction if that feels better) and come out again (that takes a few minutes too).\n\nYou can also try other ways of inducing yourself such as becoming aware of 3 things you can see, 3 things you can hear, 3 things you can feel in your body; then 2 of each, 1 of each, counting from 5 to 1 and beginning to listen. Choose one way to induce yourself, you don't need to try all of them! (In fact, it might be counter-productive!)\n\nOnce you have practiced listening a few times with the recordings, you may want to shorten them to speed up your induction, or even practice without playing them back at all. On the other hand, if you like using the recordings, there is no reason to stop! Being able to guide yourself does not mean you have to! (NB. You may wish to use the following to help you re-enter your process, this will also shorten your induction if you already know what to do.)\n\nAs you come out of the process ask yourself what you learned needed warmth, what needed to be protected, what you need to do differently to be more in accord with truth and love and life. Is there something you want to explore more fully or a capacity you want to build? And most importantly, what can you carry with you as you move forward from this? If you identified something you needed to do differently, make a plan with yourself to do that thing. The more specific you can be, the more likely you are to change: \u201cIf _________ (fill in the cue for the old pattern), then I will do ________ (fill in one small action that will begin to change the pattern).\u201d Then check back later and see how you are doing \u2013 sleeping, relating, functioning, etc.", "7c3b16f1bf1f27a53db15ac8f80c184ea8c73c4cf77112f336af83d2e4b2b905"], ["HG22-refix", () => "The weekly deeper practice\n\nIt\u2019s good to do this once or twice a week, though more is fine. It doesn\u2019t have to be very intense but it is good to start from Higher Self or at least a neutral witnessing place. It\u2019s also good to bring in some adult function to make sure nothing is being bypassed and so that at the end of the exercise, when the experience is over, there is the possibility of coming out completely and doing whatever normal thing needs doing.\n\nIf possible, it\u2019s good to do the normal thing immediately after the exercise, so that the subconscious sees that the adult\u2019s actions have been heard. Otherwise, the dishes won\u2019t get done.", "920bb2f6fd301330b9daa8b470474789d869883b490b53a9737c10409e3f7c1f"], ["HG23-refix", () => "Capacity before content\n\nNOTE: If it is not medically safe, or if you are panic stricken, sleep deprived, nauseated, deeply destabilized, manic, psychosis like, or chemically overwhelmed, do all you can to stabilize and then ask for what your subconscious needs you to know. It is not ready for you to know if you need to destabilize to know what it is! Ask for capacity and not content!\n\nWhat to do if your Subconscious Mind Knows Something You Don\u2019t Want to Know. It may have to do with your sexuality, a grief, trauma, family issue, betrayal, shame, vocation, relationship, medical issue, spirituality, addiction, identity, moral issue, or whatever.\n\nDon\u2019t bully your subconscious mind into telling you what it is by saying things like:\n\nWhy won\u2019t you just tell me? What are you hiding? Tell me right now! I command you to tell me what it is!\n\nThis usually leads to flooding, panic, false certainty, confabulation, dissociation, and a really, really bad day. If you are flooded, then you can\u2019t use your adult capacities to be able to consider different options, to reality test, to plan, to choose differently. Work on your regulation and get support before proceeding. The subconscious may be silent until your Adult is able to regulate, get support, be humble, and proceed in a way that does not blow your Adult out of the water. Ask the parts what they need for your Adult to be able to know what it is:\n\nDo I need to know what it is, or do I need to work on capacity? What can be done to make my conscious mind 5% better at knowing what it is? Can you tell me what it is in a symbolic way without full revelation? Can you tell me what to do to be safe without telling me what it is? Do you need me to get support in order for you to tell me what it is? If so, what kind of support? Who can I go to?\n\nConsider saying: \u201cDear Subconscious Mind, you are wise and you know things that my conscious mind is not able to know yet. Please don\u2019t rip the bandage off. Prepare my conscious mind to know what it is in a safe way. Ground me before showing me a memory. Support me before turning up the intensity. Tell me what to do next so that I can be ready for what you want me to know.\u201d\n\nREMEMBER: Just because you see something in a hypnotic state does not mean that it is literally true, especially when it comes to traumatic memories. The mind often makes images that are meaningful to you, but are symbolic. It often squashes several things together, distorts, dramatizes, and pulls from cultural sources. Just because you see it, doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s true. Get support outside to help you!", "cc23f2d30c4a11754d4a8bc6472938242821b30977fe3ccd33f1a9b962fe5129"], ["HG25-refix", () => "What not to do\n\nDO NOT: View these experiences as anything but internal happenings that need to be reality tested at all times.\n\nDO NOT: Engage in seeking \u201cdownloads\u201d of information or become obsessed with demons/jinn/Unattached Burdens or the like, until you have stabilized your life, perhaps even getting help to do so, if you are not reality testing well, or not functioning well in your life.\n\nDO NOT: Participate in self-hypnosis while operating a car, bathing, swimming, operating any equipment, supervising children, or engaged in any activity which requires active attention.\n\nDO NOT: Attempt to \u201cforce\u201d memories, to use trance to \u201cprove\u201d something happened to you, or to not get medical attention for symptoms, because you can \u201cforce\u201d them down using hypnosis.\n\nDO NOT: \u201cForce\u201d yourself to ignore your body\u2019s needs, such as eating when hungry, resting when tired, responding to pain, etc., or your emotions, such as letting yourself grieve when someone dies, feeling anger when it is appropriate, acknowledging your fears, etc., until you know more about what the signals are telling you.\n\nDO NOT: \u201cExtend\u201d the duration of altered states indefinitely or accept \u201chits\u201d of intuition as \u201creal\u201d without reality testing them.\n\nDO NOT: Allow various internal roles to get out of proportion (e.g., allow the \u201cInner Child\u201d to run your adult life, the \u201cProtector\u201d to preclude all loving relationships, the \u201cNurturer\u201d to disregard consequences to others, the \u201cLeader\u201d to ignore the needs of the \u201cChild\u201d). You are capable of analysis, as well as tenderness.\n\nDO NOT: Utilize NLP techniques to \u201cforce\u201d down \u201cprotectors,\u201d to give yourself certainty you do not have, to manipulate others, or to \u201cheal\u201d yourself when your body is telling you not to.\n\nDon\u2019t consider negative indicators (doubt, distraction, resistance, lack of response, saying \u201cNo\u201d) as good signs that the induction is working.\n\nDon\u2019t rely upon the \u201csafety\u201d of \u201cyour unconscious mind\u201d as the only safety factor in any session. Be sure you have set up clear limits, are in a safe place, and have a way to terminate the session and \u201cget out\u201d which has been tested and proven to work.\n\nDon\u2019t believe that normal physical sensations are indications of hidden trauma, illness, toxins in your body, possession, \u201cattachments,\u201d \u201ctransformations,\u201d or information from your \u201csubconscious mind.\u201d\n\nDon\u2019t believe that anything is \u201chealed\u201d in your body (neurologically, cellularly, etc.) simply because it is \u201chealed\u201d in your imagination.\n\nDon\u2019t put \u201chidden \u2018commands\u2019\u201d in yourself, nor allow anyone to do so. Even if you are consciously placing something in yourself which you wish to utilize later, be sure that you know exactly what you are doing and why you are doing it, and be sure that you CAN \u201ctake it out\u201d if you decide that you no longer wish to use it. It may not be as easy as simply saying, \u201cTake out.\u201d Nor should you allow anyone to activate these \u201ccommands\u201d in you without your knowledge, to make you do something you don\u2019t want to do, to make you into someone you don\u2019t want to be, to give you amnesia, etc.\n\nDO bring yourself completely back at the end of every \u201cwaking\u201d session, declaring that the session is over.", "7bdff950c7b3006d2bc0a7f4e76b9894c9dab0dea1070616fdc2f215dcd7085c"], ["HG26-refix", () => "When this needs more support than a guide can provide\n\nRemember, this is self-hypnosis, a relationship with yourself. If the situation calls for support, this guide isn't the right thing.\n\nIf you need help now: You may need help now if you feel in imminent danger, very confused, or unable to take care of yourself. You may need help now if you have physical symptoms (chest pain, fainting, etc.) You should seek professional help promptly if you have new or worsening suicidal thoughts, severe insomnia, new or worsening symptoms of mania or psychosis, or if dissociative symptoms are affecting your functioning. These are not problems that this guide will resolve in 4-12 weeks.\n\nYou probably don't need any more support than this: If you keep the practice shorter, make it warm, pick a small and tractable subject, make sure you come back out, and then see how it affects a specific target (anxiety, daydreaming, helping a relationship, facing a task you've been avoiding, helping you sleep, being less reactive emotionally, improving your intuitive accuracy, etc) for a week or two, and don't notice that your functioning is getting worse, or that you're getting more certain about unconfirmable memories, then you're probably doing fine.\n\nYou probably need more support if: You are experiencing recurring panic attacks, compulsions, substance destabilization, major relationship instability, etc.\n\nMethods to explore with a trained person present\n\nIf you want to deliberately do trauma-focused regression (going backwards in your memory or imagination to times when you were younger), or affect and somatic bridging (following associations from an emotional or somatic experience to find the origin of that experience, particularly if it was a traumatic experience you don't know about), or if you find that you're having substantial flashbacks or dissociative reactions, then you should do this with a trauma-informed trained person present. It's best if they're trained in the specific method you want to do. Ask any potential person what they would do and how they deal with uncertainty. Note that even if you work with a person, hypnosis is not a way of knowing what did or did not happen to you. (Both regression and affect/somatic bridging can also be used to find resources and do other things, of course.)\n\nNote that having experienced trauma, crying, and even wanting to feel difficult feelings, are not necessarily signs that you need more support than working on your own. You get to pick how wide and narrow a range you want to work in, but be aware that different people need different ranges. Pay attention to how you respond and what support you have. Feeling like you are handling it isn't a substitute for having support.\n\nNote that many guidelines for treating major trauma recommend one or more of trauma-focused variants of cognitive behavioral therapy (sometimes called cognitive processing therapy, prolonged exposure, eye movement desensitization and reprocessing, etc). Depending on the guideline and your situation, it may recommend one or the other or both. These can include self-hypnosis and inner child work. If you're working with high-risk trauma, you need a bigger container.\n\nAlways keep in mind that your functioning in ordinary life is the feedback. If you find yourself more loving, more honest, more functional, more relational, more grounded, more precise, etc. than when you started this process, keep on keeping on. If you notice that your ordinary life is becoming less stable, don't try to go deeper. Go for more sleep, more eating, more grounding, more healthy boundaries with other people, more getting support from other people, etc.", "e0e9e13cc3b93a4263e9a3d227a8df96f1630413bff8e834d419a24a9fd7382a"], ["HG27-refix", () => "Closing\n\nStart from the basis that the sub, the body, the sharp mind, and the guy who's tensed up and ready for the other shoe to drop for a long time are all not your enemies. Most of them are actually trying to help you.\n\nWhether or not you can \"get hypnotized\" very deeply is somewhat irrelevant to whether or not you can become a trustworthy adult.\n\nListen to it for as long as it takes until it's comfortable enough to move closer to you. This is easiest to do if you're making and keeping lots of small promises to the kid, so the various guards feel they can relax. Work on loving yourself in a way that your thinking doesn't object to; work on thinking in a way that your love for yourself doesn't become fantasy; work on doing this in the course of regular life so that your adult self can keep the promise.", "b16a6135be404fddaf933247608146c136db185df2bfeee9ab531cd365bf757a"], ["HG28-refix", () => "Try it in the Inner Signal app\n\nYou will need to download Inner Signal App for voice hypnosis, information, to learn the language, and for feedback on what you report. Have fun. Feel free to ask any questions you might have about what the hypnotist is doing. Self hypnosis is a great tool, but you don't need an app to do it. You may want to find someone, but it is not required to graduate.\n\nIf you\u2019re using the ChatGPT version of this app, you might want to upload a picture, drawing, poem or song to talk about instead of writing out your explanation in prose. But please make sure the file you upload can be seen or heard by the chat you\u2019re currently using! It will probably tell you that it can\u2019t see or hear the file if you\u2019ve made this mistake. Please remember that what\u2019s in the file, what it means to you, and what the app thinks it means, are three different things, and that you get to decide for yourself whether the app has interpreted it correctly \u2013 you don\u2019t have to defend your choice of medium.\n\nBear in mind that even with voice, the app is asking you what\u2019s going on for you \u2013 it can\u2019t feel your body, share a practitioner\u2019s embodied intuition, or know a response you don\u2019t report. The app is not pretending to be a skilled therapist, just helping you to learn for yourself, so that you can make better-informed choices.\n\nAlways enter this app via this page, not by bookmarking the app itself, to make sure you get the current version.\n\nPlease fill in this survey with what you\u2019ve learned, so that you have something to analyse later, and others can learn how the guide is landing in real practice.\n\nIf the guide or the app leaves a real question unanswered, please contact me here to discuss arranging a consultation.", "80cb46deac3277bd5038a0b2f1847f6eb73f62b3d17f3167e37517b6b589e747"], ["HG33-refix", () => "Appendix D: Anxiety \u2014 body first\n\nRemember that often the anxiety comes from a protector part, a part of yourself who is trying to help you, but who believes you are in danger, or may be shamed, or abandoned, or fail, or be exposed, or become sick, or rejected, or lose control, or suffer something else unbearable. Therefore, instead of an interrogation, start with yourself:\n\nAlways work with yourself by first taking care of your body, then your inner child, then some inner inquiry, and then some action:\n\nInner child love\n\nInner child love: Put a hand over your heart, and a hand on your solar plexis, and say lovingly, \u201cLittle one, you are not alone. You don\u2019t have to fix this. I\u2019m here now. The adult is listening.\u201d Don\u2019t just say the words, but say them in a way that you are talking to the inner child, who is frightened.\n\nReduced breathing / Buteyko-style breathing\n\nReduce your breathing. (NOTE: there are some good things to be said for slowing down the breathing, for some who overbreathe or are panicked, and this part is based on the Buteyko approach. But please don\u2019t force yourself to hold your breath and suffer air hunger, which is going to make you more anxious for a period. Proceed slowly.) Take small inhales through the nose, and quiet exhales, with pauses if you can. Can you quiet your breathing? STOP if you feel dizzy or experience any other medical issues.\n\nEFT tapping\n\nEFT tapping: One of the easiest ways to do EFT is to say something like, \u201cEven though I have this anxiety, I am willing to be kind to the part of me that is afraid,\u201d while you tap on your body. There isn\u2019t a ton of evidence for EFT, but there are some studies on anxiety. A 2025 systematic review found 7 randomized control trials for anxiety disorders, and noted that EFT was more effective than no intervention in a few studies. So use the evidence with caution, and know that there are first line therapies for anxiety.\n\nSomatic Experiencing\n\nSomatic experiencing: If you would like more information about somatic experiencing, or even a free intro session, please see my somatic guide . In somatic experiencing (SE), you are not thrusting into the trauma. You learn to track. So you might start by tracking, by discovering where the activation is, where a neutral place is, and then whether you can move your attention from one to the other, very slowly, like a snail.\n\nGendlin Focusing\n\nGendlin Focusing: Focusing is another approach where you work with your body. You might say to yourself, \u201cWhat is the felt sense of this whole anxiety?\u201d Don\u2019t answer with your head; let your body come up with a vague sense of the whole anxiety. Then ask, \u201cWhat would this felt sense like me to know?\u201d Try a word or a phrase and see if it feels good. But also see if what the word or phrase says is true of the situation. The word may feel ok, but say something that doesn\u2019t fit the situation, or vice versa. Use the words and the body to mutually correct one another.\n\nBody supports\n\nWork with the body. Sometimes the mind is too activated for meditation to help, so you may need to work directly with the body to calm it down. Maybe get a massage, or massage a foot, your scalp, a temple, or the back of the neck, the top of a shoulder, etc. (Avoid massaging the front of the neck. Also avoid massaging injured or numb body parts, or bruised, inflamed, or recently surgically operated on areas, or varicose veins. Also stop if the massage makes the anxiety symptoms worse, or makes you feel bad in any way, such as painful, dizzy, tingly, etc.) There are many other somatic approaches you can try, like heat, pressure, a weighted blanket, darkness, your favorite calming music, a careful use of a massage gun, etc.\n\nYou may find that you settle down with some of these things: warmth, darkness, favorite music, massage, a weighted blanket, some breathwork, a favorite object, technology you use to relax, etc.\n\nI have a page on my ZHoly3O product, which is ozonated charcoal, and I use a bit of this \u201choly water\u201d as one of the things that helps me relax. (See the mention of Blushield on that page, too.) But neither one of those products are necessary. All you really need is to stabilize yourself, and then listen to the messages from your inner realm, reality test those messages, and then take some action.\n\nA script you could use for anxiety is:\n\nAnxiety script\n\nWhere am my body? What are my feet doing? How am I sitting in the chair? How am I breathing? How is my body in the room?\n\nIf you can hear me, I want you to know that I am here. Thank you for alerting me. You don\u2019t have to scream. I got your message.\n\nNow if there is something we need to do, show me what the first thing is that we should do, right now. And if there is nothing we need to do, help my body stand down, and know that I am not going to abandon you, but I am also not going to worship you. I am going to listen to you, reality test what you are saying, and then take some action.", "b30eb5af40508b8219749a409bb00480d9362f56b2de524856f035628620ff5e"], ["HG34-refix", () => "Appendix E: Is the daydream helping or replacing your life?\n\nSometimes daydreaming is something that your subconscious mind is doing to help you. It is simulating an idea or event to help you digest grief or teach you something. The very act of daydreaming may be helping you to access your creativity or allowing your subconscious to show you a potential future. Sometimes your subconcious will show you things that you may be afraid of. Sometimes it will show you what you want.\n\nOther times daydreaming may be taking you away from your life in a detrimental way. It may be that you are escaping reality and are addicted to fantasies rather than the real life. You may be dissociating or obsessing about romantic partners or escaping from being an adult.\n\nHow do you know which it is? Simply ask yourself if the daydreaming is taking you closer to life, with more clarity, love and ability to take action or if it is taking you away from life, in a repetitive and craving way that takes you away from living your life.\n\nIf it is helping you then simply ask yourself what the guidance is and how you can use it.\n\nIf it is taking you away from life then change your body position, open your eyes and ask your subconscious to help you. Simply say to yourself, \u201cDear subconscious if what you are showing me is helpful then please also show me the helpfulness in it. If what you are showing me is a way of avoiding dealing with life then please show me in a gentle but structured way how to deal with life as it is right now.\u201d\n\nThen ask yourself what it is that you need to do in \u201creal\u201d life that you are avoiding by daydreaming.\n\nYou may need to send a text message or stop sending text messages. You may need to clean up your room, eat, sleep, deal with grief, create, apologize, leave, tell the truth, make a plan, get help, get back to a task that you were supposed to be doing, stop chasing love that is not available to you etc.", "53040ba4e2f6534501637d82ed68fd225e37e72d3ab88a499b115f2b8e5e7d1b"], ["HG35-refix", () => "Appendix F: Self-trust, outside guidance, and oracle-like states\n\n[Please see how to use synchronicity as a cue, above.]\n\nOne of the issues here is that people vary dramatically in how suggestible they are, both internally and externally, to various types of suggestion, and different people vary in how suggestible they are in different states. Different types of suggestion (commands, imagery, music, metaphors, spiritual, etc) can be very different for different people. So there are definite advantages to both having someone work with you, and doing things yourself. Being able to follow up immediately, to correct something in real time, to have a line of communication with protectors, etc.\n\nThat said, self hypnosis may be the best way of talking to your subconscious on a day to day basis. If you\u2019re dealing with particularly complicated trauma, blind spots, dissociation, destabilisation, or relational wounds that need another nervous system, skilled outside support may be best.\n\nFinding a hypnotist who can work with you\n\nWhat they are trained in (what they can treat) How they use hypnosis What they will do if things don't \"fit\" (if they are treating trauma, did they have specific training on trauma and dissociation? Having hypnosis certifications doesn't mean they are trained in trauma care)\n\nWhat has/hasn't worked for you in the past How direct you want them to be What kind of touch (if any) you are ok with What kind of imagery (if any) you are ok with What you want them to do if you want them to stop What they will do if things go unexpected during or after the session What they do if you aren't sure if something is a memory or not How they will do the full return (coming out of hypnosis) at the end of the session You should be able to be firmly encouraged, but not forced to continue if you don't want to.\n\nThen afterwards, check in about what was actually done, regardless of what you might call the method. Ask the person why they did what they did, if they told you in advance. Did you agree to it? How did the person respond to you? Keep in mind that just because something made you uncomfortable, it doesn't mean it was \"bad,\" but if they saw your discomfort as meaning that you needed more of it, that might be something to look into. You might even be able to use this app or ask around to see if someone can tell you what the things they did meant. They probably won't be able to tell you if the person was \"certified\" in them or not, though. Then you can decide if you want to try learning to do self-hypnosis, using both, or find someone else. Those are all good options.\n\nWhen the subconscious speaks like an oracle\n\nYour subconscious is amazing at picking up on things your conscious mind isn't getting. Whether it's anticipations, reading patterns, or just picking up on uncanny things, it's good to respect what your subconscious is picking up on. But just because your subconscious gives you an image or tells you to do something, that doesn't mean you need to treat it like an order.\n\nEspecially if it's a big thing, or something that can't be easily undone, slow it down to the scale of the thing. Look at it with your adult's eyes, and take it to council.\n\nThe council \u2014 internal first, then outward\n\nAsk your child, your adult, your conscious mind, your subconscious mind, your intuition, your analytical mind. But if it's bigger than all of those, ask outside of yourself, too. The bigger and more un-undoable something is, the more you want to reach outside.\n\nAsk people who love you, people who are like you, people who have done what you are thinking of doing. Sometimes it is right to go it alone, but I would suggest making it the last step, after you've tried to get council.\n\nOn the other hand, it is possible to give your power away. Seeking counsel can quietly turn into abdicating to an authority figure. Another person doesn\u2019t get automatic trust, or automatic dismissal.\n\nSometimes you need the support of your peers. In Hearthwork, the concept is that you give each other equal time, warmth, confidentiality, and acceptance of \u201cno\u201d as an answer, and you act for each other as Nurturer and Protector, but not as Guide. Then you reverse roles. Sometimes, with a question asked carefully and at the right time, your peers can help you hear your own Guide more clearly, but they don\u2019t interpret what you experience.\n\nForgiveness without bypass\n\nYou say that we cannot \u2018force\u2019 ourselves to forgive someone and that it has to come out of a place of understanding for it to not be a bypass etc. But how can we let go of the anger if we cannot or do not want to always be angry? How do we hold all of this, together? The fact that all of this can be true at the same time is so important.\n\nA helpful understanding to come to, is that while their actions were harmful, in a sense, they could only make the moves they made, given their accumulated nature at the time (conditioning, history, pain, capacity, etc). This doesn\u2019t negate that harm was caused, holding someone accountable, allowing for consequences, working on making different moves now, etc. It simply helps us come to a place where we aren\u2019t expecting something from someone that they can\u2019t give. It doesn\u2019t make their limitations matter any less.\n\n\u201cYou don\u2019t have to forgive before you\u2019re ready. I won\u2019t use spirituality to silence your pain. And I won\u2019t build our whole life around this wound forever.\u201d\n\nSome questions that may be helpful to ask when coming to a place of forgiveness, while still holding all of the above:\n\nWhat actually happened? What was the impact? What boundaries need to be set? What shaped the other person(s) into someone capable of that harm? What is theirs? What is mine? What does accountability require? How can I let this go, without denying any of the above?\n\nFor self-forgiveness, name what you did, without taking responsibility for what wasn't yours. Let the remorse register the harm, or how it went against your values, without making yourself a permanent criminal.\n\nTake responsibility, feel the remorse, then rectify if you can, and then let it go. Be specific about the action you took, and the impact it had, feel the remorse, do what you can to rectify or keep it from happening again, and then stop holding yourself hostage.", "1c9f0c712e92362d1ae6f19e693e119c9a6e563ef039911b5b7fa0d68301ec90"], ["HG36-refix", () => "Appendix G: Altered states\n\nNB: I am NOT saying use these. However, many people attempt to do things for the first time such as self hypnosis, contact with their inner child, contact with their Higher Self etc when they are in a mind altered state.\n\nIf you do use them, be aware you don't want to force a revelation out of the state but instead use it to help you do things in your regular life.\n\nIf you have had an opening in the past, the key is to recognize that it is different to have an experience, access it in a particular state and access it in your day to day life. It is great that it has opened but if the child can't take it in, then\n\nUse phrases such as; Help me to ground. Help me to only take that which I can take in. Help me to remember love. Help me to come back when the time is right. Help me to take one change into my regular life.\n\nYou should NOT use self hypnosis to; Keep you in that state forever Get memories to come up Make yourself afraid to do things Not sleep Override things that your body needs Not talk to people\n\nIf you are doing this in an altered state of consciousness and it is helping you not to love, not to ground, not to be honest, not to sleep, not to communicate, not to do regular life things, you need to STOP trying to go deeper and work on integrating what you have.\n\nStabilize before you interpret\n\nSelf hypnosis can be extremely powerful when you are in a different state of consciousness (such as on loveyhuasca, meditating, in a lucid dream, when you are grieving, when you are using sexual energy, when you are praying, when you are not sleeping, or with other plant medicines etc). Sometimes you can open your mind up faster than you can process it as an adult.\n\nThe problem comes in when people are in a different state of consciousness, they think it must mean something. Sometimes it is your inner child, sometimes it is a Protector projecting their fear, sometimes it is your shame/grief/anger/longing etc coming up for help, but sometimes it is just your body's way of saying it doesn't like what is happening, the environment is chaotic, you didn't sleep well, or for any number of other reasons it might not make sense. Just because you get a picture that scares you, it might not be true. Just because you have a bad feeling, it doesn't mean it is a lesson. Just because you get a download in nice lighting, that doesn't mean you should believe it.\n\nInstead of trying to interpret what is going on, ask yourself;\n\n\u201cWhat kind of problem is happening?\u201d", "f48ba94ac3350360bcb7229f31d184f5aa1bd48d10b837bdb2e5493988424ac8"], ["HG40-refix", () => "Appendix K: Sources and further reading\n\nEverything in this post is my own, especially if it involves adaptations like the one I'm doing here where I am combining body orientated work and hypnotic work. This is not a validated form of treatment at this time. These instructions are not necessarily needed during the practice, they're here for your perusal.\n\nLearning, entering, and returning\n\nLearning to learn, how to get in and out\n\nHealing the Divided Self , Maggie Phillips and Claire Frederick, (1995) pp 24-27, 45-50, 83-90, covers a lot of aspects of this post, such as interactive hypnosis, helping the subject learn how to learn by using other senses, learning self hypnosis, making sure the subject comes back at the end, etc. However, this is a professional clinical book, not a self help book, so be careful about trying to use the procedures used with the cases, etc in this book for solo work (the same applies to historical information it contains). Also, Adam Eason's work with Benjamin Parris in the International Society of Hypnosis, as well as his article about self hypnosis , should be a useful thing to read (especially the parts that talk about how to learn to learn when you're directing it yourself, and about whether you need another person to help you, and using recordings to help you, etc.)\n\nIndirect language and re-entry cues\n\nFor information about using indirect hypnotic language patterns, such as pacing, utilizing, metaphor, and associational cues, etc, see Healing the Divided Self , Phillips and Frederick, 1995, pp 53 - 57, 96 - 100, as well as nimja's tutorial on hypnotic language patterns , and his tutorial on triggers . The information on these techniques comes from these sources, not because they are necessarily validating the validity of some aspects of NLP, or because he wrote or endorses this guide (nimja did not write or endorse this guide), but because I was adapting the language used for my own purposes, and I deliberately used a sequence that would be easy to use for re-entry.\n\nBody awareness and changing the amount of contact\n\nNOTE: Some of the information in this post comes from In an Unspoken Voice , Peter Levine, 2010, especially ch 5 and 7, as well as ch 3 and 4 of Freedom from Pain , Levine and Maggie Phillips 2012, and ch 4 of Healing Trauma , by Levine. These sources talk about the key concepts of tracking what is happening in the body, resources, titration, pendulation, and the range of foci available when working, from sensation and imagery to behavior, emotions, and meaning, etc. This is not done from a position of \"here is what you need to do to physiologically fix it\", but here are some things you can try, etc.\n\nInner-child care and adult capacities\n\nFor information about all of these things, see Inner Child Self-Love Reparenting Guide . The practices in this post are designed to match with those in the guide, but include some elements of learning to get in and out of self hypnosis, as well as other helpful language, and making sure you come back at the end, etc.\n\nSome of the information in this post is taken from Healing the Divided Self , Phillips and Frederick, 1995, pp 148-153, 171-174, about renurturing work, and how it can be combined with somatic work, and how to develop capacities for nurturing, etc. For information about attunement, and how every child is different and needs to be responded to differently, see Trauma Through a Child's Eyes , Levine and Maggie Kline, especially ch 4, 5, 10, etc, as it talks about actual kids (and this guide is applying this to how to respond to younger feeling states within an adult). The sequence for doing this with borrowed adulthood and the arrangement of 3 functions of adulthood, etc, is not from these authors, however.\n\nInner speech and putting experience into words\n\nNot everybody has an inner voice , Nedergaard and Lupyan 2024, is not about self hypnosis adaptations, but about people with different amounts of inner speech. The questions in the quick start are not a validated way of seeing if you can do self hypnosis, but are simply there as a practical way of seeing for yourself how you are.\n\nMemory, support, and choosing a practitioner\n\nChapter 7 of Trauma and Memory , by Peter Levine, 2015, contains useful information on this. This US Veterans Administration website , contains useful general information about hypnosis, such as the fact that it can be very strong and should be carefuly used, and that it may result in false memories. This ASCH website , contains information about the usefulness of getting certified in hypnosis, etc. Links are available for these and other useful groups in the evidence and specialist sections.", "a42004fac5be11fb44b85eca2822ebd321f37a6eee690573d730b04c43c0d91e"]];
